# Git + PR first (no ad-hoc rsync)

WW360 product changes go through **branches and PRs into `develop`**. Staging must not become the only copy of work.

## Do

- Start each topic from a clean `origin/develop` → `feature/<topic>`
- Commit, push, `gh pr create --base develop`
- When the user pivots topics: park WIP (`wip/` branch or labeled stash), then new branch from `develop`
- Deploy staging from a **git ref** (merged `develop` or an explicit PR branch checkout on the VM)

## Do not

- `rsync` a dirty local tree to staging as the normal ship path
- Keep stacking unrelated WIP on long-lived kitchen-sink branches (e.g. landing-slider)
- Leave “works on staging” uncommitted

## Override

Only rsync if the user **explicitly** asks for an emergency hotfix — then commit and open a PR with the same changes immediately.

